    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0676" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9454/8–1445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)<anchor n="95" xml:id="d443-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-14T20:00:00-04:00">August 14, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2535. See Dept’s cirtel concerning Japanese archives.<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d443-f2"/> Request Swiss to communicate following to the Japanese
                    Govt: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Japanese Govt will immediately instruct its diplomatic and consular
                            offices in neutral countries to surrender custody of all property and
                            archives to representatives of Allied powers.</p>
                        <p>The Japanese Govt will likewise authorize the appropriate government
                            protecting its interests to relinquish diplomatic and consular property
                            and archives to the custody of Allied powers in belligerent
                            countries.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d443-f1" n="95" type="source" xml:id="d443-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Moscow, and London as telegrams 1259, 1836, and 6912,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d443-f2" n="96" xml:id="d443-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
